1835		proof over the source law remains open; the real-part auxiliary above
1836		does not establish it. See \cite{gap:qpbt_subline-claims-line-marginal}.
1837		Write
1838		$W^{x,z}_{a,b} = \hat{Q}^{x,z}_{a,b}
1839		- \hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Point},Z),z}_{b}
1840		\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Point},X),x}_{a}$
1841		and apply the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality to the difference of the two
1842		sides. The first factor is at most $1$ because
1843		$\sum_{f_X,f_Z \,:\, f_X(x)=a,\ f_Z(z)=b}
